# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build and tool artifacts.
#
# Measured before writing this: of the untracked output, 90.6 MB is tool logs,
# 40.3 MB is raw reports and 8.1 MB is generated scripts -- all reproducible by
# re-running a flow.  The actual dataset (per-run metrics, provenance, and the
# aggregated CSVs) is 1.7 MB.  So results/ uses an allowlist: ignore everything,
# then re-admit the data files by name.  New tool artifacts are then ignored
# automatically instead of needing a new rule each time a flow is added.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Liberty cache, generated testbenches, VCDs, simulator binaries.
build/

# OpenROAD is built out-of-tree into here; the submodule itself is tracked by
# commit, and its own build dirs are its own business.
third_party/install/

__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# results/ : allowlist
#
# NOTE the ordering. `results/**` must come first, `!results/**/` re-admits the
# directories (git cannot descend into an ignored directory to find the
# negations), and only then do the file negations take effect.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
results/**
!results/**/

# Per-run parsed metrics -- what every table in docs/ is built from.
!results/**/metrics.json
!results/**/metrics_tcl.json

# Which RTL and which constraints produced each run.
!results/**/provenance.json

# Aggregated dataset and sweep manifests (results.csv, summary.csv,
# matrix_*.json).
!results/*.csv
!results/*.json

# Sweep driver logs are small (tens of KB) and useful for reconstructing what was
# run.  Tool BUILD logs are not measurements and belong under build/ instead --
# openroad_build.log lived here briefly at 251 KB, which is why this is called out.
!results/*.log
results/*_build.log

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately NOT ignored, to be explicit about it:
#   benchmarks/**/*.sv              hand-written RTL, the point of the repo
#   benchmarks/**/constraints/*.sdc hand-written constraints -- note these share
#                                   filenames with Genus-written SDCs that land
#                                   under results/, which is exactly why the
#                                   ignore rules above are scoped to results/
#                                   rather than written as a bare *.sdc
#   benchmarks/**/*.tcl             directives.tcl / common.tcl are inputs
#   flows/**                        flow scripts
#   scripts/**                      harness
#   docs/**, papers/**              write-ups and references
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Archived gf180 dataset (superseded by nangate45 as the primary PDK, kept for the
# cross-technology comparison). Same allowlist as results/.
archive/results_gf180/**
!archive/results_gf180/**/
!archive/results_gf180/**/metrics.json
!archive/results_gf180/**/metrics_tcl.json
!archive/results_gf180/**/provenance.json
!archive/results_gf180/*.csv

# calibration (r01 achieving 0.58 ns against a 2.27 ns "calibrated" period), but they
# sit at off-grid periods and must not be pooled with the real matrix. Same allowlist.

# Benchmarks dropped 2026-08-23 as uninformative (the tool already solved them, or
# they duplicated another case). Kept out of the active suite but not deleted; the
# RTL stays tracked, the measurement artifacts follow the results/ allowlist.
archive/dropped_results/**
!archive/dropped_results/**/
!archive/dropped_results/**/metrics.json
!archive/dropped_results/**/provenance.json

# Advisor Slack transcript: private correspondence, deliberately not published.
slack_*.md

# Third-party papers: read locally, never redistributed from this repository.
papers/

# Working notes and agent instructions: local only.
CLAUDE.md
ideas
ideas.md
ideas-ethan.md
ideas-honed.md
